cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Debian 13 hardening framework, selective AppArmor userns profile, ephemeral KVM/QCOW2 sandbox orchestrator, or 43-control auditor in research or security audits, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Techdim Debian 13 Hardening Framework & Ephemeral KVM Sandbox (Kether_1)"
abstract: "Reproducible six-layer Zero Trust and CIS Benchmark Level 2 hardening framework for Debian 13 (Trixie, Kernel 6.12 LTS) hosts executing autonomous AI agents without breaking unprivileged user namespaces (userns) or eBPF. Provides deployable sysctl, AppArmor 4.x selective userns, default-deny nftables, ordered lossless auditd (-b 8192, -e 2), DNS-over-TLS, OpenSSH 10 configurations, an ephemeral QCOW2/KVM sandbox orchestrator, a strongly typed 6-layer metrics collector, and a 43-control CIS/BeyondCorp auditor."
